# Forensics & Response: field kit USB tooling and disk/image forensics.
# Field kit host tooling (snapshot-fieldkit-prep / -import). snapshot-fieldkit
# recommends these, and recommends are off, so they are listed here:
# - exFAT for the stick (mkfs.exfat); dosfstools (FAT32) is in the installer list;
exfatprogs
# - udisks2: the import mounts the stick read-only as the operator, through
#   udisksctl, without root.
udisks2
# fdisk, util-linux, jq, rsync and busybox are already in the base image.
# Evidence handling on both arches: The Sleuth Kit CLI (mmls, fsstat, fls,
# icat, tsk_recover) and TestDisk/PhotoRec (Autopsy's carver uses photorec).
sleuthkit
testdisk
#if ARCHITECTURES amd64
# Runtime for the vendored Autopsy (amd64 only; docs/vendoring.md). Recommends
# are off, so everything it loads is listed:
# - libtsk_jni.so (vendor/recipes/sleuthkit-jni.sh, built against this pin):
libewf2
libafflib0t64
libvhdi1
libvmdk1
libsqlite3-0
zlib1g
# - its Solr script probes the port with lsof (procps is in the base):
lsof
# - the media viewer plays video through the system GStreamer:
gstreamer1.0-plugins-base
gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly
gstreamer1.0-libav
gstreamer1.0-x
gstreamer1.0-gl
gstreamer1.0-alsa
gstreamer1.0-pulseaudio
#endif
